{
 "about": "Texts with a `--!>` or a `--->`, at which GitHub's HTML parser ends a comment before the `-->` at which CommonMark ends it, and the forms of the end of a comment, by place: inline, as a block, in a quote, a list item, a heading, a setext heading, a cell, a footnote, a `div`, a `pre` and `details`, in nested quotes and lists, a quote that holds a table, link text, an image description and emphasis, with CRLF row ends, before a quoted value of a tag, an end tag, an `img alt`, a `video`, an `rp`, a `relative-time`, a void tag in `svg`, a drawn `pre`, a link reference definition and the elements that GitHub's filter takes out or shows as text; indented code and a table with a second row too. Each with the marker words that GitHub's renderer (gh api -X POST markdown with mode gfm, 2026-11-23) shows and hides, as a headless Chrome read the page; GitHub's script draws a date in place of a relative-time that has a `datetime` and a diagram in place of its source, the page shows the body of a closed details after a click, and the description of an image is its alt text.",
